title: 'statement-store: hold a statement while no routing target can receive it'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    On the v2 DHT path a node holds a statement while none of its routing targets can receive it
    yet. A full peer becomes a routing target when its substream opens, but it takes statements
    only after its affinity filter is applied. A statement propagated in that gap was skipped for
    the peer and left without a hold, so the retention sweep could remove it before the peer's
    initial sync read it. Now the statement stays in the store until the initial sync of a routing
    target passes it.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
